      "content": "Irregular pressure spikes in the hydraulic circuit of your 2022 F-150 transmission are a serious sign, and you're right to be concerned. These fluctuations are often caused by a failing or clogged valve body, which is where the pressure is managed. Another common culprit is low or contaminated transmission fluid, which can lead to inconsistent hydraulic operation. You might also want to check the torque converter lock-up clutch components, as they can introduce erratic pressure demands.",
